abstract: >-
  Zero-Mathlib Lean 4.35.0 proofs of all-n counting identities for 2-blade
  nullities in the explicit Cayley-Dickson sign table, for all signatures
  (Pillar 1 and the midpoint law) or the Euclidean signature (Pillar 2); the
  bound n+5 for coordinate right-multiplier families in the Euclidean CD_n,
  which equals the Hurwitz-Radon number for n = 3, 4, 5 and is smaller for
  n >= 6; and finite certificates for sedenion, pathion and chingon
  coordinate subsets, including a re-verification of de Marrais's 7
  box-kites. The Lean statements concern the sign table and block counts;
  that these counts equal annihilator dimensions is a lemma proved in the
  paper. The bound r_max(CD_5) = 14 and the CD_6-CD_8 tables rest on exact
  computation outside Lean. The divisibility of nullities by 4 is the
  2-blade case of a theorem of Moreno. The title is that of the frozen
  v1.0.0 manuscript; its "dimension-64 rupture" refers to coordinate
  right-multiplier families in the Euclidean CD_n only. See ERRATA.md.
keywords:
